                <pb facs="0261" n="1221" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1221"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 110.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Data in the case of Shields and Wilson.</hi></head>
                <p>Gulie Shields and Isaac Wilson, charged with the murder of Modesto Maldonado.
                    Offense committed at Fort Clark, Kinney County, Texas, on or about December 31,
                    1888.</p>
                <p>The defendants are Seminole Negro-Indians, ages about fifteen and sixteen
                    respectively. They left Fort Clark about the time of the murder, crossed the Rio
                    Grande river into Mexico, and went to the Seminole reservation near Santa Rosa
                    in the State of Coahuila. They are not aware of the existence of an indictment
                    against them, and will hardly change their names.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John T. Rankin</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Marshal.</hi></signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                Antonio, Texas</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-08-14"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 14,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
